al4bet.zip  -- complete alphabet plus other neat things (Andrew Kunze).
amn.zip     -- contains a building inspired by the "Amnesia" demo (Todd Porter)
chess.zip   -- a chess board and metallic pieces (Todd Porter)
choppe.zip  -- a helicopter, with moving parts! (Ed Schindler?)
dactyl.zip  -- a tribute to Virtuality's "Dactyl Nightmare" (Todd Porter)
dactyl.ogr  -- another Dactyl Nightmare world, created with OGRE (David Boeren)
multi.zip   -- some deck chairs, in multiple versions (Ed Schindler)
ncad.zip    -- some objects created using a modified Northcad 3D (Todd Porter)
pool.zip    -- a nice swimming pool with deck and chairs (Ed Schindler)
prims.zip   -- some geometric primitives (Bernie Roehl)
sega3d.zip  -- the Sega circuit, rendered in 3D (Todd Porter)
superq.exe  -- Some superquadrics (Mark Pflaging)  [self-extracting]
tesseract.plg - a tesseract (Andrew Hudson)
x29plg.zip  -- the X-29A jet fighter

The file prims.zip contains a few geometric primitives (sphere, cone,
truncated cone, cylinder, torus) as well as a short IRIT input program
that generates them (you'll need IRIT and the irit2plg converter to make
use of the program).

